      overload: 0.05
      lunehymnBoost: 0.15
      attuneEase: 0.03
      ritualHarm: 2
    plagues:
    - id: dragons-bane
      name: Dragon's Bane
      description: A sickness that ignores a dragon's armored scales and corrupts the Pure Light pathways beneath them, the channels that feed its enchantments. Tuned to one Fundamental Frequency, it finds a creature near-immune to every other illness and undoes it.
      folklore: the scale-rot
      hosts: []
      dissonanceAt: 0.2
      chance: 0.3
      lethality: 0.4
      duration: 3
      spread: 0.1
      immunity: 6
    - id: slime-blight
      name: Slime Blight
      description: An acoustic virus that opens Dissonance Blooms in a slime's Light channels and cancels the standing waves that give it shape. Past a threshold the collapse is sudden and total, and a living slime becomes lifeless protoplasm.
      folklore: the melting
      hosts: [ice-slime, snow-slime, lake-slime, marsh-slime, saltwater-slime, grassland-slime, mineral-slime, forest-slime, leyline-slime, dead-zone-slime]
      dissonanceAt: 0.15
      chance: 0.5
      lethality: 0.6
      duration: 2
      spread: 0.25
      immunity: 4
    - id: lantern-gutter
      name: Lantern Gutter
      description: A narrow-band resonance sickness that locks onto the Lanternback's hide-light and drains it. The glow gutters, the herd goes dark and still, and the weakest do not rise again.
      folklore: the dimming
      hosts: [lanternback-grazer]
      dissonanceAt: 0.15
      chance: 0.5
      lethality: 0.45
      duration: 2
      spread: 0.15
      immunity: 4
    - id: veil-blight
      name: Veil Blight
      description: It unsettles the Coherence-Binding Tissue in a Moonveil Moth's wings until the beat falls out of phase, and whole veils drop from the air in a single night.
      folklore: the falling sickness
      hosts: [moonveil-moth]
      dissonanceAt: 0.15
      chance: 0.5
      lethality: 0.55
      duration: 2
      spread: 0.15
      immunity: 4
    - id: chorus-fever
      name: Chorus Fever
      description: A sickness tuned to the Choir Cicada's song. One singer out of phase pulls the rest after it, and the chorus sings itself to death.
      folklore: the wrong song
      hosts: [choir-cicada]
      dissonanceAt: 0.2
      chance: 0.5
      lethality: 0.5
      duration: 2
      spread: 0.15
      immunity: 4
